======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  No new law.  The candidate 'missing mass = A x hot gas' is closed (slope 0.6, coefficient falls x3-4 from groups to clusters).
  What the 9,830 eRASS1 systems do show on the framework's kernel is a residual eta = M_dyn/M_MOND at R500 that is constant, 2.1 +/- 0.3
  (0.08-0.11 dex catalogue scatter), from 3e13 to 2e15 Msun.  That constancy is algebraically the statement f_b(R500) = g_N(R500)/(eta^2 a0),
  i.e. the measured f_gas ~ M^(1/3) scaling of hot systems with its coefficient set by a0 -- a restatement of a known scaling, not a new
  regularity, and it fails as a radial law inside clusters (gas fractions rise outward, the relation says they should fall).  The optical
  group test (Milgrom 2019's sample) is inconclusive without per-group gas masses.  Both footings agree at every line.

